1
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:14,960
These days, we use credit cards more and more and they all look almost identical.

2
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:20,240
But money is still with us, in coins and banknotes.

3
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:29,140
The designs are different and all over the world we can see examples of really interesting and beautiful banknotes.

4
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:37,380
The designs usually celebrate the country – its history, its geography, its animals and birds.

5
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:42,320
Here are some examples of banknotes from different parts of the world.

6
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:45,700
Mexico

7
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:49,060
In Mexico the currency is the peso.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,140
The smallest banknote is 20 pesos, and the biggest is 1,000 pesos.

9
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:06,160
One side always has the face of a famous person from Mexican history and the other side has well-known places in the country.

10
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:14,160
On the $500 note there is a portrait of the famous Mexican artist Frida Kahlo.

11
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:17,949
Europe

12
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:25,340
Many countries in Europe use the euro, but the banknotes are exactly the same for each country.

13
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:33,180
On one side, there is a picture of a gate, window or entrance, and on the other side, a bridge.

14
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:39,114
The pictures represent different kinds of architecture from all over Europe.

15
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,060
Turkey

16
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:49,930
In Turkey the currency is the Turkish lira, and there are six different banknotes.

17
00:01:50,780 --> 00:02:01,260
Each one shows Kemal Atatürk, the founder of the Turkish republic, on the front side, and another famous figure from Turkish history on the other side.

18
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:05,500
Brazil

19
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,520
The currency in Brazil is the real (plural, reais).

20
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:25,580
The notes are in different colours, but they all have a picture of the Effigy of the Republic (a national symbol of Brazil) on one side, and various animals, birds and fish on the other side.

21
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:32,860
One of the most beautiful is perhaps the R$50 note, which has a picture of a jaguar.
